.TH SED 1
.SH NAME
sed \- stream editor
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B sed
.RB [ -n ]
.RB [ -g ]
.RB [ -d ]
.B -e
.I command
.RB [ -e
.IR command ...]
.RI [ file ...]
.br
.B sed
.RB [ -n ]
.RB [ -g ]
.RB [ -d ]
.B -f
.I cmdfile
.RI [ file ...]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.I Sed
is a partial port of Plan 9's own stream editor: it applies a script
of editing commands to each line of each
.IR file
(standard input if none given) and writes the result to standard
output.
.PP
Options:
.TP 10
.B -n
Suppress the default output of each pattern space; only lines an
.B p
command (or a substitute's
.B p
flag) explicitly prints are written.
.TP
.B -g
Treat every substitute command as globally flagged, as if
.B g
were given on each one.
.TP
.B -d
Enable debug tracing of the compiled command list.
.TP
.BI -e " command"
Add
.I command
to the script; may be repeated.
.TP
.BI -f " cmdfile"
Read the script from
.I cmdfile
instead of
.BR -e .
.SH SOURCE
.B /appl/cmd/sed.b
